# FRDM-IMX95 Foundries lab

## User runs (do not spawn shell subagents for these)

- `./scripts/flash-imx95-uuu-only.sh prep|check|run`
- `./scripts/capture-frdm-serial.sh`
- `uuu`, `systemctl`, `/dev/ttyACM*`, `nc localhost 2000`
- `fioctl` downloads

## Agent does

- Read `logs/frdm-serial-*.log`, `docs/lmp-frdm-workflow.md`, `docs/imx95-foundries-emmc.md`
- **SSH to the board** (`fio`/`fio`, sudo `fio`) to validate on real hardware — see `embedded-engineer` skill lab section
- **Serial via ser2net** (`nc localhost 2000` @ 115200) — prefer over `/dev/ttyACM*` in agent shells
- Advise BSP / `meta-dynamicdevices-bsp` / factory-integration changes; **confirm before manifest pin / CI trigger**
- Edit repo files without requiring sandbox `all` unless user explicitly asks
- **Ask** whether to monitor CI/flash and iterate on failure vs stop and report

Full embedded workflow (CI guardrails, intake, evidence): `~/.cursor/skills/embedded-engineer/SKILL.md`

## Boot loop

Foundries CI → fetch target → flash (SW1 0,1) → serial via ser2net (SW1 1,0, user power-cycles) → iterate.

**SW1 / mode:** Until HW automation (Michael/Ollie), agent infers programming vs run mode (USB phase, serial) and **asks you to set SW1 + power-cycle** when wrong for the next step.

Default target unless stated: ask user or use latest from their message.
